  "coverage_meaning": {
    "finite_test": "A complete finite-test object must be exact-file-specific: unique decision dependency, strongest contrary explanation, confirmed/refuted consequences, canonical public-record route and an explicit primary-source route or route gap. A recorded custodian/organ is only a candidate and may not be treated as legally competent, empowered or obliged to act; any consequence remains conditional on exact competence and a lawful route. The contrary explanation remains hypothetical and attributes no act to the candidate without a primary source. Canonical record type precedes a mixed Stream substring when assigning the UI-only family. Generic registry-maintenance, source-retrieval or record-correction boilerplate cannot count. NOT_LOCATED remains permissible and structural coverage is not primary-source or merits completion.",
    "receipt_knowledge": "Classification coverage and positive evidence are separate. Each of nine institutional axes—transmission, material received/inventory, referral, registration, file incorporation, recipient attribution, substantive examination, decision use and cross-file acknowledgement—requires its own status, bilingual basis, bilingual limitation and controlled source or source-gap object. Every positive grade must cite the exact episode field that supports that axis; episode-and-axis overrides are required where a global default would cite unrelated text. Transmission and referral are independent. Institutional handling cannot establish actor-specific receipt or knowledge.",
    "actor_specific": "Actor-specific receipt and knowledge remain non-positive unless an actor-specific source identifies the person, material or act, time and permissible evidential scope.",
    "fiscalia": "Twenty-four public Master Register rows—21 exact and three unresolved references—receive separate source-attributed material, received-inventory-gap, direct/context proceeding, related-asset-gap, referred, actually-examined, response, cross-file, unitary, contrary and unanswered dispositions. Only reviewed event-to-matter relationships may support the eight profiled matrix rows. A ninth response episode profiles the separate DP 1901/2026 judicial file outside the matrix.",
    "routing": "Master Register, exact trace and isolation routes are required for every public exact ID. Dedicated narrative dossiers are a separately counted optional positive route.",
    "case_prism": "The finite-test layer does not add the 54 no-coordinate proceedings to a shared proposition or lane."
  },
